<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="c8b0b41d">&lt;p&gt;
    The cutover go/no-go checklist considers all criteria essential to making the decision to move forward with the
    transition. This will also consider criteria for moving forward with a phase or moving to the proceeding phase.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The criteria are typically categorized into broad headings such as:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Processes are proven
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Systems are ready
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Business is ready
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        People are ready
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Data is ready
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Technology infrastructure is proven
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="a3b90017"></attribute>
